### Step 1: Bug Scenario Image and Root Cause Analysis

#### Bug Scenario Image Description
The image shows a custom `BizFormItem` component that wraps a `FormItem` and injects a custom label DOM structure. The business code uses a custom label (with an icon) and passes it to `FormItem`. The `FormItem` is expected to use the label for error messages (when `useLabelForErrorMessage` is enabled), but because the label is now a React node (not a string), the error message label fallback does not work as intended.

#### Root Cause
- The current implementation of `getLabelForErrorMessage` in `src/form/item.jsx` only uses the `label` prop if it is a string. If the label is a React node (e.g., a span with an icon), it returns `null`, so the error message label cannot be customized.
- The feature request is to allow an explicit `errorMessageLabel` prop, so the business code can specify what label to use for error messages, regardless of the DOM structure of the visible label.

